for d in items:
    if d['id']=='1970-226.8':
        d['statement']=r'For the group-action site of a connected Lie group \(G\), the sheaf of locally constant functions with values in a fixed discrete abelian group \(A\), with trivial action on the coefficient group, gives \(H^*(BG;A)\). For the smooth equivariant-function sheaf of a continuous Banach representation, site cohomology agrees with the differentiable group cohomology denoted \(H_{\rm alg}^*(G;E^\infty)\) by Geronimus.'
        d['reconstruction']=r'The coefficient group is abelian; the two comparisons use distinct coefficient sheaves. Connectedness is retained for the announced Lie-group comparison. No general identification of Lie-algebra and classifying-space cohomology is inserted.'
    if d['id']=='1970-228.11':
        d['statement']=r'For the Heisenberg group with circle center \(T\), let \(\Gamma\) be the compatible lift of a principal lattice, with \(T\cap\Gamma=\{1\}\). Inducing from \(T\Gamma\) by the character \(\chi(t\gamma)=t\) gives the irreducible lattice realization of the Schrödinger representation with \(U_t=tI\). Induction from the discrete subgroup alone, or replacement by an arbitrary nontrivial central character, does not have this stated multiplicity-one conclusion.'
        d['reconstruction']=r'The full center and its tautological character are essential. Principality is relative to this central weight; it does not give multiplicity one for every character \(t\mapsto t^m\).'
    if d['id']=='1970-215.5':
        d['verification']='read the result'
        d['confidence']='high'
        d['fate'] += r' The original Introduction, p.~145, explicitly says the equality was not proved there; Definition 1.6 on p.~149 gives the zeta-regularized torsion.'
    if d['id']=='1970-215.6':
        d['fate'] += r' The original Ray--Singer Introduction, p.~145, independently confirms its conjectural status in 1971 \citep{raysinger1971torsion}.'

